{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And did not bear them.</b> We find also in another place ארץ in masculine: \"יסוב כל הארץ כערבה\" (Zechariah 14:10). \"בעברת ה׳ צבאות נעתם ארץ\" (Isaiah 9:18). And in another verse androgynous: \"אבל אומללה ארץ\" (Isaiah 33:9)." "<b>For their possessions were great.</b> And this matter caused the quarrel."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {0 "The lemma refers to ולא נשא אתם in Genesis 13:6, where אתם is masculine though it refers to הארץ, which is normally feminine; Chizkuni cites instances of ארץ taking masculine or both masculine and feminine forms."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:04:05.841205614Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}